bin  boot  dev  etc  home  lib  lib64  media  mnt  opt
proc  root  run  sbin  srv  sys  tmp  usr  var



1️⃣ /bin    
Contains essential user commands. 
( Examples commands : ls cp mv cat )

2️⃣ /sbin    
Contains system administration commands. 
( Examples: shutdown reboot fdisk )

3️⃣ /boot  
Contains bootloader and kernel files needed to start Linux.   
(Examples:  Linux kernel GRUB bootloader)

4️⃣ /dev
Contains device files.
In Linux, devices are treated like files.
( Examples: disks, terminals, USB devices)

5️⃣ /etc
Contains system configuration files.
Very important directory.
( Examples: network configs, passwd files, ssh configs )

6️⃣ /home
Contains home directories of normal users.
Example: ( /home/ubuntu, /home/Bharath )

7️⃣ /root
Home directory of root user.
( Example: /root )

8️⃣ /lib and /lib64
Contain shared libraries required by binaries.
Similar to DLL files in Windows.

9️⃣ /usr
Contains user applications and utilities.
Subdirectories:
Directory	   Purpose
/usr/bin	   User commands
/usr/lib	   Libraries
/usr/share   Shared docs/files
( Example: ls /usr/bin 
Contains: python, vim, git )

🔟 /var
Contains variable/changing data.
Examples: logs, cache, spool files )

1️⃣1️⃣ /tmp
Temporary files.
Applications store temporary data here.
Usually cleaned automatically.
( Example: touch /tmp/test.txt )

1️⃣2️⃣ /proc
Virtual filesystem containing process and kernel info.
Not real files on disk.
( Example: cat /proc/cpuinfo )
Shows CPU information.

1️⃣3️⃣ /sys
Provides kernel and hardware information.
Used for system tuning and device management.
( Example: ls /sys )

1️⃣4️⃣ /run
Stores runtime process information.
( Examples: PID files, sockets )
Created during boot.

1️⃣5️⃣ /mnt
Temporary mount point for manually mounted filesystems.
( Example: mount /dev/sdb1 /mnt )

1️⃣6️⃣ /media  
Mount point for removable devices.  
( Examples: USB drives, CD-ROMs )

1️⃣7️⃣ /opt
Optional third-party software. 
( Examples: Tomcat, custom applications Example: /opt/tomcat ) 


1️⃣8️⃣ /srv 
Data served by services.   
( Examples: FTP web server data )
